<title>USA: ThermoSpectra acquires Park Scientific.</title>
<headline>ThermoSpectra acquires Park Scientific.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>ThermoSpectra Corp said on Thursday it has acquired all of the shares of Park Scientific Instruments Corp for approximately $17 million in cash, subject to a post-closing adjustment.</p>
<p>ThermoSpectra, a publicly traded unit of Thermo Instrument Systems Inc, said it assumed Park Scientific stock options, exercisable into 183,940 shares of ThermoSpectra common stock with a weighted average exercise price of $3.44, for an aggregate value of approximately $2 million.</p>
<p>Park Scientific makes scanning probe microscopes, including vacuum, ambient air, and liquid cell systems, the company said.</p>
